For every $n\ge1$ there is a constant $K_n\ge1$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \max_{0\le t\le1}r(t)\le K_n\int_0^1r(t)\,dt
\end{equation}
for every real polynomial $r$ of degree at most $n$ which is nonnegative on $[0,1]$.

Let $P\in\Pn$, let $M>0$ be such that $\norm P\le M$, and take $u_1,\ldots,u_n\in B_X$ and $f_1,\ldots,f_{n-1}\in B_{X^*}$. For $1\le i<n$ and $t\in[0,1]$, let $S_i(t):X\to X$ be the linear map
\[
 S_i(t)x=(1-t)x+tf_i(x)u_i\qquad(x\in X).
\]
Suppose that, for some $E\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \Rea P\bigl(S_1(t_1)\cdots S_{n-1}(t_{n-1})u_n\bigr)\ge M-E
 \quad\text{for every } t_1,\ldots,t_{n-1}\in[0,1].
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 |\check P(u_1,\ldots,u_n)|\ge M-H_n\sqrt{ME}.
\end{equation}

